281 - 170\n$$\n\nNext, we carry out the subtraction:\n\n![](images/32/32ceb366008206a2d765e3507a6b1d1d60682c407e9eb26ea90d230159a0377a.svg)\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n281-170 = 111.\n$$\n\nHowever, since our answer must be negative, we need to change the sign of the answer above. \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n170 - 281 = -111.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064255 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049429 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064255 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186064527 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064255 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186064570 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064255 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186064629 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064255 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186433314 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064255 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186433317 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064255 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186433318 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064255 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186433319 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064255 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186433320 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064255 #edb/ref 1039 "Subtracting a Positive Number From a Non-Negative Number" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064255 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186063935 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064255 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "6a3c970b-4086-52ef-ac0f-2b8c3d72fd51" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064256 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049516 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064256 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186064485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064256 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186064526 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064256 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186064528 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064256 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186433315 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064256 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186433316 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064256 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186433321 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064256 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186433322 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064256 #edb/ref 1039 "Subtracting a Positive Number From a Non-Negative Number With Larger Numbers" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064256 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186063936 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064256 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "f1c51da0-7569-50c0-b405-c74419d47ef3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064418 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186065131 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064418 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186065132 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064418 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186065133 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064418 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186065134 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064418 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064418 #edb/ref 1045 "Subtracting a Positive Number From a Smaller Positive Number" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064418 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186065131 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064418 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048911 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064418 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064418 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "af1ad9c9-eddf-59bb-aedf-24a165cae134" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064526 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186061386 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064526 #edb/ref 1069 "q-170960" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064526 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064526 #edb/ref 1071 "$12-36=${{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064526 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b8f6a9f4-4f58-50a4-818d-d75ee08e55ed" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064526 #edb/ref 1074 "Since $36$ is larger than $12,$ the answer will be negative.\n\nWe start by solving an easier problem:\n\n$$\n36-12\n$$\n\nNext, we carry out the subtraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  & \\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n36-12=24.\n$$\n\nHowever, since our answer must be negative, we need to change the sign of the answer above. \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n12-36=-24.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065131 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186065132 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065131 #edb/ref 1061 188374 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065131 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e99d8d22-f103-5560-a608-35f0957133f4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065131 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186065412 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065132 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186065133 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065132 #edb/ref 1061 188375 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065132 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a7e8a41f-1f30-5c54-b22b-c51e7a5efd82" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065132 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186064255 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065133 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186065134 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065133 #edb/ref 1061 188379 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065133 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "12b96179-bf32-5136-bbf1-e7631a656dfb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065133 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186065413 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065134 #edb/ref 1061 188380 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065134 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9f2475d1-01ac-524a-9a5e-a1adfdc797a2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065134 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186064256 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065412 #edb/ref 1064 "When we subtract a positive number from another positive number, we move towards the left on the number line. \n\nFor example, let's consider the following subtraction problem:\n\n$$\n3 - 5\n$$\n\nTo subtract $5$ from $3,$ we start at $3$ on the number line and move $5$ places to the left.\n\n![](images/57/57ac1fe7a28ae5fefadf900d2276d499cdccf01df48b819b0aafa5347a2ec506.png)\n\nWhen we do this, we land at $-2.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n3-5 = -2.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065412 #edb/ref 1065 8029 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065412 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "8af27dde-6aa4-5067-84f8-9538f1acaa18" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065412 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065413 #edb/ref 1064 "It is impractical to use number lines to subtract large numbers. \n\nHowever, a neat trick makes subtracting a positive number from a smaller positive number very easy!\n\nAs an example, let's consider the following subtraction problem:\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}{37}} - {\\color{blue}{68}}\n$$\n\nSince $68$ is larger than $37,$ the answer *must be negative*.\n\nWe start by solving an easier problem: subtracting the numbers *in the reverse order*. In our case, the reverse problem is\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}{68}} - {\\color{red}{37}}.\n$$\n\nNext, we carry out the subtraction:\n\n![](images/db/db192e5c1f089e3d4cc2a7b1238392e44a7ba36bff99345a997042c16ebc304f.svg)\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}{68}} - {\\color{red}{37}} = 31.\n$$\n\nHowever, since our answer must be negative, we need to change the sign of the answer above. \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}{37}} - {\\color{blue}{68}} = -31.\n$$\n\nAnd that's it! \n\nLet's use the same idea to subtract two three-digit numbers." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065413 #edb/ref 1065 8030 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065413 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "d7dbb60e-47d5-56db-981a-145c532f7ace" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065413 #edb/ref 1067 "Subtraction With Larger Numbers" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433283 #edb/ref 1080 "312" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433283 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433283 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "13042cd9-3fe1-5a6e-9f68-9d984f61c24d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433284 #edb/ref 1080 "-312" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433284 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433284 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1770c383-61fb-5018-b6c5-fdbcc32171fc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433285 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433285 #